# fstab — Orange Pi 3 LTS (Allwinner H6, arm64) headless appliance.
#
# Installed-root targets: microSD, the onboard 8GB eMMC (unlike the Zero 2/
# Zero 3 siblings this board HAS one, and the mainline sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts
# enables its mmc2 node), or USB — no NVMe (the H6's quirky PCIe is not usable
# in mainline; see specs-orangepi3-lts/README.md's storage confidence notes).
# Like the Frite/Orange-Pi-5 builders, this image produces LIVE/
# INSTALLER ISO media + a stage4 tarball — there is NO build_img/.img assembly
# step here. The LIVE flavor boots a squashfs root ephemerally (this fstab is
# largely inert there; / is the live overlay). The INSTALLER flavor
# (install-orangepi3-lts.sh) partitions the target medium AT INSTALL TIME and
# rewrites the LABEL=/PARTUUID device columns below for the medium it actually
# wrote, so the installed system mounts the right partitions. The placeholder
# device paths below are replaced at install time; do not rely on them literally.
#
# <device>              <mount>  <type>   <options>                              <dump> <pass>
LABEL=OPI3L_BOOT     /boot    vfat     defaults,noatime,nosuid,nodev,noexec   0      2
LABEL=OPI3L_ROOT     /        ext4     defaults,noatime                       0      1
tmpfs                /tmp     tmpfs    defaults,nosuid,nodev,noexec,size=128m 0      0
tmpfs                /run     tmpfs    defaults,nosuid,nodev,mode=0755        0      0

# zram swap: this is a small, cheap appliance board (a single 2GB LPDDR3 SKU
# per the vendor's spec sheet — see the README); a zram helper is configured at
# first boot by the builder (mirrors La Frite's 512MB SKU handling) rather than
# baked as a fixed swap partition here, keeping the image byte-similar to its
# Zero 2 template.
